# GitHub API Token for Portfolio Contributions
# 
# This token is used to fetch your GitHub contribution calendar data.
# Without a token, you're limited to 60 requests/hour per IP.
# With a token, you get 5,000 requests/hour.
#
# To create a token:
# 1. Go to GitHub → Settings → Developer settings → Personal access tokens → Tokens (classic)
# 2. Click "Generate new token (classic)"
# 3. Name it: "Portfolio Contributions"
# 4. Select scope: ✅ read:user (required for public contribution data)
# 5. Optional scopes: ✅ public_repo (if you want to show repo stats)
# 6. Generate and copy the token
# 7. Paste it below
#
# Note: This token is exposed in the browser (NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix), so only use read-only scopes.
# Never use admin or write scopes with NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.

NEXT_PUBLIC_GITHUB_TOKEN=your_github_token_here
